# SilentLayer workspace key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and replace the value with your own secret.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The key is the single shared secret behind every image this build produces:
# it is the input to HKDF, which derives both the AES-256-GCM envelope key and
# the DCT scatter seed. Two builds with different keys cannot read each
# other's images.
#
# REQUIREMENTS
#   - Use a HIGH-ENTROPY RANDOM value, at least 32 bytes.
#   - Do NOT use a memorable passphrase. HKDF is a key-derivation function, not
#     a password hash: it is deliberately fast and has NO work factor, so a
#     human-chosen phrase can be brute-forced offline very cheaply.
#   - Generate one with:
#
#       node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# WARNING
#   Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the shipped JavaScript bundle. That
#   means anyone who obtains the built site has the key and can decrypt any
#   image made with that build. This is a shared-secret design, not per-user
#   encryption. Keep the build private.
#
#   Never commit `.env`. It is already listed in `.gitignore`.
#
# CHANGING THE KEY
#   Changing this value makes every previously created image unreadable. There
#   is no key rotation and no version field in the envelope, so this is a
#   one-way door. Keep a backup of the key if you need old images to stay
#   readable.

VITE_SILENTLAYER_WORKSPACE_KEY=replace-me-with-a-random-32-byte-secret
